        .title About
        .blurb Hello! My name is Stephanie Claudino Daffara, but my friends call me Ste. I started off as a filmmaker, became a computer scientist, and have finally now mixed the two into what I am today: an immersive experience creator. From AR museum exhibits to XR integrated Theatric performances, I am always searching for new ways to tell narratives that enhance the delivery and unfolding of stories.
        .blurb I am a recent graduate from UC Berkeley with a degree in Computer Science. The classes I took focused on Graphics and Machine learning; the research projects I participated in involved Data Science and Visualization; and the collaborations I did with professors involve Augmented Reality and Art. For fun I led an Immersive Cinema (360-degrees) Research and Production group. Today I am still involved with the University, contracted as a VR and AR expert for a diverse number of projects.
        .blurb In the same way that I practice furthering my own knowledge, I actively seek projects and research teams that focus on the intersection of technology, education and the arts pushing for a reality where everyone has easy access to education and the mental, emotional and financial freedom to follow their creative passions.
        .blurb So if you are looking for a hand in software development, design or immersive experiences lets talk:
